# Story 74: Spawning an Agent (45s)
# Hook: One command, one prompt, and your agent is alive.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-074-spawning-an-agent.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
One command, one prompt, and your agent is alive.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Launch rysh and double-press Escape into rysh mode to run the agent system commands.

[00:08.0 --> 00:18.0]
Use ##agent spawn, then a name, then the system prompt in quotes. That prompt defines the agent's whole personality and job.

[00:18.0 --> 00:28.0]
Spawn as many as you need. Here's a second agent for writing tests.

[00:28.0 --> 00:40.0]
Then ##agent list shows every agent with its current status -- active, deactivated, or working a prompt right now.

[00:40.0 --> 00:45.0]
Spawn, name, prompt, list. That's the whole lifecycle of an agent.

